From 273f0ea2b2dca9bdd5f6399b96b2e4769a550b8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades] Adjust display resolution: a video in the mode of its
 own size
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A setting next to Kodi's "Adjust display refresh rate" (Player > Videos, the same level; off by
default): a video goes out in a mode of the display of its own size, at the refresh rate that Kodi
chose for it, where the display has one. Kodi changes the size for a video only where a whitelist of
the user lists modes of other sizes (System > Display > Whitelist, Expert); its default whitelist
holds the modes no smaller than the menus, so a film of 1920x1080 on a TV with the menus at
3840x2160 went out at 3840x2160, scaled by the graphics card. With the setting on it goes out at
1920x1080 and the TV scales it.

- After Kodi's whole choice (the exact rate, twice it, 3:2, the whole multiples, the 25p and 30p
  rules and a mode at the rate at another size), the mode of the video's size at the refresh rate
  chosen (within Kodi's 0.01 Hz), of the same kind (interlaced or not, the same 3D layout): the
  nearest size by Kodi's own rule (MatchesMode(), now in VideoSizeMode.h), then the nearest rate.
  Where the display has none, Kodi's choice. The cadence never changes.
- Not with a whitelist of the user (it chooses the modes and their sizes), and not for native Dolby
  Vision: the HDMI policy of the tunnel takes CTA 1080p (drm_dvbridge.h), but the engine of the bridge
  is made for a raster of 3840x2160 (the pixel of each bit of the metadata, its tiles of 16 lines,
  the level 5 area, the check of its bytes) and so is the window of native output
  (DVPlaybackPolicy.h). The help says, in plain words, that the graphics card enlarges a 1080p Dolby
  Vision video. HDR10, HDR10+, HLG, Dolby Vision played as HDR10 or SDR and 3D take the mode of their size.
- Where "Video at its own rate with VRR" takes a video, Kodi's choice ends before this, in the mode
  of the menus.
- Named as Kodi's translations name the setting next to it: "Ajustar resolución de la pantalla"
  (es_es), "Ajustar la resolución de la pantalla" (es_ar), "Ajustar la resolución de pantalla"
  (es_mx). Core #62145, #62146; Estuary #54145, #54146.

Checked: a host test (video_size_test.cpp: the modes of the LG C5 and the G60SD as Kodi listed them,
the rate, the kind, the order, when it looks, Kodi's size rule) with its mutants; the changed files
and the sources that include them compile with the commands of the image's build. Not run on a GPU.
